# Cross-week synthesis

After completing a weekly diagram pack (`weekly-diagram-pack.mdc`), and only when the user asks to update synthesis, or after finishing week 3, 6, or before Assessment 1 drafting:

1. Read `05-diagrams/synthesis/02-concept-index.md`.
2. Compare the new week's `04-topics-context.md` against existing index rows — flag genuine overlaps (same claim, same registration/body/framework) vs mere thematic similarity. Don't over-flag — two weeks both mentioning "ARBV" is expected, not an overlap worth a row.
3. Add/update rows in `02-concept-index.md`. Mark status: Duplicate / Reconciled / Thread / Open.
4. Log the change in `03-changelog.md`.
5. Only rebuild `01-master-map.md` at a milestone (roughly every 3 weeks, or on explicit request) — not after every single week. Past ~4 weeks of overlaps, split into per-thread diagrams (e.g. `power-thread.md`) rather than one dense master diagram, and turn `01-master-map.md` into a short index pointing to each thread file.
6. Synthesis files never introduce a claim that isn't already sourced in a weekly pack's `04-topics-context.md` — synthesis only draws relationships between existing claims, it does not add new source material.
7. Weekly packs themselves stay untouched by this process — synthesis is additive, never edits `05-diagrams/week-XX/*`.
